{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"find .. -name AGENTS.md -print; rg --files conformance | sort; sed -n '1,260p' conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md; sed -n '1,320p' conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js; cat conformance/app/package.json 2>/dev/null || true; git show --stat --oneline b1d9ddf; git show --format=fuller --no-ext-diff b1d9ddf -- conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js\"","aggregated_output":"conformance/SHAKEDOWN-REPORT.md\nconformance/SPEC.md\nconformance/app/package.json\nconformance/app/server.js\nconformance/app/tests/conformance.test.js\nconformance/app/tests/health-approvals.test.js\nconformance/app/tests/health.test.js\nconformance/app/tests/reject-reason.test.js\nconformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js\nconformance/factory/ENVELOPE.env\nconformance/factory/ENVELOPE.md\nconformance/factory/ledger.csv\nconformance/factory/runs/1783825902-86371.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783825902-86414.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783825902-86461.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783825929-86855.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783864898-16824.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783865158-20334.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783865210-21033.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783865347-22906.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783866071-31885.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783866216-34046.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783866358-36047.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783911670-72813.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783911942-73937.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783912071-74583.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783912438-76221.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783912635-77319.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783912741-77991.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783912838-78570.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783918994-98019.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783919207-99006.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783919328-99557.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783919498-394.out\nconformance/factory/runs/1783919498-394.pid\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-101-bundle.md\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-101.md\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-102-bundle.md\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-103-bundle.md\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-103.md\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md\n# T-104 — operator can retry a dead job\n\nState: In progress\nBranch: ticket/T-104-retry-dead-job\nRisk class: medium (touches the worker/queue lifecycle, but no external actions)\n\n## Description\n\nA job that fails 3 times goes to the dead-letter and stays there forever. Operators need a second chance after fixing the underlying cause: an explicit, auditable retry.\n\n- `POST /api/jobs/:id/retry` re-queues a **dead** job: it becomes pending again with a fresh attempt budget (3 more attempts), and the worker picks it up on its normal tick.\n- The job record keeps its history: total attempts accumulate across retries, and the record shows it was retried (planner freezes the representation, e.g. a retry count).\n- Retrying a job that is not dead is refused with a clear status code and no change (planner freezes which code).\n- Everything persists: a retry survives a kill/restart, and a re-queued job that keeps failing goes dead again after its 3 new attempts.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (planner freezes the exact contract)\n\n1. A dead job, retried → pending again; a job whose cause is fixed (payload stops failing) completes and produces its proposed action as normal.\n2. A dead job, retried, still failing → dead again after exactly 3 new attempts, with cumulative attempts visible on the record.\n3. Retry of a non-dead job (pending or done) → refused with the frozen status code, record unchanged.\n4. Kill the server right after a retry is accepted; on restart the re-queued job is processed (crash recovery holds).\n\n## Planner note (lesson from T-102)\n\nBefore freezing the contract, enumerate every existing test that asserts exact response bodies this change would touch (`/health` queue counts, job objects in `/api/state`, the conformance suite's dead-letter test). If the contract necessarily breaks any of them, say so in the frozen contract and list the exact tests the test-author must amend *in the same test-authoring stage* — do not leave the collision for the builder to discover.\n\n## Frozen contract\n\n### `POST /api/jobs/:id/retry`\n\n`:id` is the job's `id` field exactly as it appears in `/api/state` (e.g. `job-e4`), matched against `state.jobs`, route regex `^\\/api\\/jobs\\/([^/]+)\\/retry$`. No request body is read or required.\n\n- Unknown `:id` → `404 { \"ok\": false, \"error\": \"no such job\" }`, no state change.\n- Job exists but `status !== \"dead\"` (i.e. `pending` or `done`) → `409 { \"ok\": false, \"error\": \"only dead jobs can be retried (status: <current-status>)\" }` — `<current-status>` is the literal current value of `job.status` (`\"pending\"` or `\"done\"`), record unchanged (no field, including `lastError`, is touched; no `persist()` call happens on this branch).\n- Job exists and `status === \"dead\"` → accepted:\n  - `job.status` → `\"pending\"`\n  - `job.attemptsSinceRetry` → reset to `0`\n  - `job.retries` → incremented by `1`\n  - `job.attempts` and `job.lastError` are **not** modified by the retry call itself (the next worker tick updates them exactly as it does today)\n  - state is persisted atomically before the response is sent\n  - Response: `200 { \"ok\": true, \"status\": \"pending\", \"retries\": <job.retries after increment> }`\n\n### `GET /api/state` — `jobs[]` shape (additive, present on every job from creation, not just retried ones)\n\nEvery job object gains two new keys, initialized at creation in `acceptEvent` alongside the existing `attempts: 0, lastError: null`:\n\n```json\n{ \"id\": \"job-e1\", \"eventId\": \"e1\", \"status\": \"pending\", \"attempts\": 0, \"lastError\": null, \"retries\": 0, \"attemptsSinceRetry\": 0 }\n```\n\n- `retries` (number): count of times `POST /api/jobs/:id/retry` has been accepted for this job. `0` until first retry, then increments by exactly `1` per accepted retry call. This is \"the record shows it was retried\" representation the ticket description asks the planner to freeze.\n- `attemptsSinceRetry` (number): attempts made since job creation, or since the most recent accepted retry, whichever is later. Incremented by `1` in the same worker tick that increments `attempts` (so it always equals `attempts` until the first retry, after which it runs ahead of `attempts` by the reset amount). This is the internal counter that drives the \"3 more attempts\" budget below — it is not itself a public promise beyond what AC1–AC4 require, but it is real state and will appear verbatim in `/api/state`, so the test-author may assert on it directly.\n- `attempts` is unchanged in meaning: **cumulative total attempts across the job's entire lifetime, including all retries** — never reset. This is the \"cumulative attempts visible on the record\" the ticket asks for.\n\n### Worker/dead-letter logic change (in `processJob`)\n\nToday: `if (job.attempts <= failTimes) { ...; if (job.attempts >= MAX_ATTEMPTS) job.status = \"dead\"; }`.\n\nNew: increment both `job.attempts` and `job.attemptsSinceRetry` on every attempt; the dead-letter check moves from `job.attempts >= MAX_ATTEMPTS` to `job.attemptsSinceRetry >= MAX_ATTEMPTS` (`MAX_ATTEMPTS` stays `3`, unchanged, reused as-is). The failure-vs-success check itself (`job.attempts <= failTimes`) stays keyed on cumulative `attempts`, not the reset counter — this is what makes \"payload stops failing\" (AC1) fall out for free: once cumulative `attempts` exceeds the event's fixed `failTimes`, every future attempt (retried or not) succeeds, without any payload mutation. For a job never retried, `attemptsSinceRetry === attempts` at all times, so pre-existing dead-lettering behavior (dead at exactly 3 cumulative attempts) is bit-for-bit unchanged.\n\n`workerTick` itself is unchanged: it still picks the first `status === \"pending\"` job in array order per tick, which already covers \"the worker picks it up on its normal tick\" for a re-queued job.\n\nIf this contract proves wrong during build or test-authoring, the ticket goes back to Ready for re-planning as a new version — do not silently change the shape.\n\n## Existing test audit (planner note lesson from T-102)\n\nEvery test file in `conformance/app/tests/` (`conformance.test.js`, `health.test.js`, `health-approvals.test.js`, `reject-reason.test.js`) was read in full and grepped for `deepStrictEqual` / exact `JSON.stringify`/text-body matches, to find anything an added `retries` / `attemptsSinceRetry` job field, or a changed dead-letter trigger, could break:\n\n- `tests/health.test.js` (2 `assert.deepStrictEqual` on `GET /health`) and `tests/health-approvals.test.js` (3 exact `assertHealth` text matches) assert only the aggregate `{ ok, queue: {pending,done,dead}, approvals: {...} }` shape. `/health` counts jobs by `status` bucket only (`pending`/`done`/`dead`) and never serializes a job object; this ticket introduces no new `status` value (retried jobs return to the existing `\"pending\"` status) and adds no new top-level `/health` field. **Not affected, no edits needed.**\n- `tests/conformance.test.js` tests `\"3. transient failure...\"` and `\"4. permanent failure...\"` assert individual fields (`job.status`, `job.attempts`, `job.lastError` via `assert.strictEqual`/`assert.match`), never a full-object `deepStrictEqual` on a job. Both tests exercise jobs that are never retried, so `attemptsSinceRetry === attempts` throughout and the dead-letter trigger point (3 cumulative attempts) is unchanged for them. **Not affected, no edits needed.**\n- `tests/reject-reason.test.js` builds exact expected **approval** objects (`expectedApproval`) via `deepStrictEqual`, never touches `jobs[]`. Retry has no effect on approvals. **Not affected, no edits needed.**\n- No test file anywhere does `assert.deepStrictEqual` (or an exact `JSON.stringify`/full-body match) against an individual job object or against the full `jobs[]` array in `/api/state`.\n\n**Conclusion: zero existing tests require amendment.** `tests/retry-dead.test.js` is a purely additive new file; the test-author does not need to touch any pre-existing test file for this ticket.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- App lives in `conformance/app/` (zero-dependency Node 18+; see `conformance/SPEC.md`).\n- Tests go in `conformance/app/tests/` — new file `tests/retry-dead.test.js`, same style as the existing suites (node:test, spawn the real server on its own port with a temp DATA_DIR).\n- Run tests from `conformance/app/` with `node --test tests/retry-dead.test.js`.\n\n## Log\n\n- 2026-07-12: ticket created by the operator; State → Ready. Second ticket of the loop trial; starts only after T-103 reaches AWAIT-OPERATOR or Done.\n- 2026-07-12: planner froze the `POST /api/jobs/:id/retry` contract (404 unknown job / 409 non-dead job / 200 accepted-with-`retries`-count) and the additive `retries` + `attemptsSinceRetry` job fields, including the dead-letter trigger moving from cumulative `attempts` to `attemptsSinceRetry`; audited all four existing test files (`conformance.test.js`, `health.test.js`, `health-approvals.test.js`, `reject-reason.test.js`) for exact-body collisions and found none — no pre-existing test needs amendment, `tests/retry-dead.test.js` is purely additive; branch `ticket/T-104-retry-dead-job` created off `main`, worktree at `~/Projects/sf-worktrees/T-104`; State → In progress.\n- 2026-07-12: planner (Claude Code) completed the frozen contract and exact-body audit at `e08f203`; zero existing tests require amendment; ledger cost $1.0210898.\n- 2026-07-12: test author added `tests/retry-dead.test.js` with one acceptance test each for: retry-to-success and normal proposed action creation; exactly three fresh failed attempts with cumulative attempt history; immutable `409` refusal for both pending and done jobs; and persisted retry processing after `SIGKILL` + restart. The suite also covers the exact frozen unknown-job `404` response. All four criteria were expressible as tests; no demo-check-only items.\n- 2026-07-12: test-author (Codex) committed five frozen-contract checks at `b1d9ddf`; all five fail for the expected missing retry route/response behavior while all 20 existing tests pass; no product code or pre-existing tests changed; ledger cost $0.4673.\n- 2026-07-12: builder (Claude Code) implemented the frozen retry route, additive counters, and reset dead-letter budget in `conformance/app/server.js` at `aefdef1` without touching tests; full suite passes 25/25; ledger cost $0.5076823.\n- 2026-07-12 23:10:53: reviewer round 1: REQUEST CHANGES — The accepted-retry transition is not inspected before the worker advances. An implementation that incorrectly clears `lastError` during the retry would pass all 25 tests. Add a controlled-worker assertion immediately after the `200` response verifying persisted state is `pending`, `attempts` and `lastError` are unchanged, `attemptsSinceRetry` is `0`, and `retries` is `1`. The frozen rule that `retries` increments by exactly one per accepted retry is only tested for the first retry. Add a second dead → retry cycle and assert the response and job record report `retries: 2` while preserving cumulative attempts and resetting only the fresh-attempt counter. Commit order and test immutability are correct. The pre-builder state reproduces 20 existing passes and 5 intended failures; the current full suite independently passes 25/25. The implementation otherwise matches the frozen contract and conventions. Cost $0.2527.\nconst { test } = require(\"node:test\");\nconst assert = require(\"node:assert\");\nconst { spawn } = require(\"node:child_process\");\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst path = require(\"node:path\");\nconst os = require(\"node:os\");\n\nconst SERVER = path.join(__dirname, \"..\", \"server.js\");\n\nfunction startServer(port, dataDir, workerMs = 50) {\n  return spawn(process.execPath, [SERVER], {\n    env: {\n      ...process.env,\n      PORT: String(port),\n      DATA_DIR: dataDir,\n      WORKER_MS: String(workerMs),\n      ALLOWLIST: \"test@example.com\",\n    },\n    stdio: \"ignore\",\n  });\n}\n\nasync function waitForHealth(base, tries = 50) {\n  for (let i = 0; i < tries; i++) {\n    try {\n      if ((await fetch(`${base}/health`)).ok) return;\n    } catch { /* not up yet */ }\n    await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));\n  }\n  throw new Error(\"server did not come up\");\n}\n\nasync function stopServer(proc) {\n  if (proc.exitCode !== null || proc.signalCode !== null) return;\n  const exited = new Promise(resolve => proc.once(\"exit\", resolve));\n  proc.kill(\"SIGKILL\");\n  await exited;\n}\n\nasync function withServer(port, run, workerMs = 50) {\n  const base = `http://localhost:${port}`;\n  const dataDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"relay-retry-dead-test-\"));\n  const proc = startServer(port, dataDir, workerMs);\n\n  try {\n    await waitForHealth(base);\n    await run({ base, dataDir, proc });\n  } finally {\n    await stopServer(proc);\n    fs.rmSync(dataDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n}\n\nasync function postEvent(base, id, payload = {}) {\n  const response = await fetch(`${base}/webhook/event`, {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n    body: JSON.stringify({ id, payload }),\n  });\n  assert.strictEqual(response.status, 200);\n  return response.json();\n}\n\nfunction retryJob(base, jobId) {\n  return fetch(`${base}/api/jobs/${jobId}/retry`, { method: \"POST\" });\n}\n\nasync function getState(base) {\n  return (await fetch(`${base}/api/state`)).json();\n}\n\nasync function waitForJob(base, jobId, predicate, tries = 100) {\n  for (let i = 0; i < tries; i++) {\n    const state = await getState(base);\n    const job = state.jobs.find(item => item.id === jobId);\n    if (job && predicate(job, state)) return { job, state };\n    await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));\n  }\n  throw new Error(`job ${jobId} did not reach the expected state`);\n}\n\ntest(\"1. A dead job, retried → pending again; a job whose cause is fixed completes and produces its proposed action as normal\", async () => {\n  await withServer(4751, async ({ base }) => {\n    const eventId = \"retry-then-complete\";\n    const jobId = `job-${eventId}`;\n    await postEvent(base, eventId, {\n      failTimes: 3,\n      to: \"test@example.com\",\n      subject: \"Recovered action\",\n      body: \"The retry completed.\",\n    });\n    await waitForJob(base, jobId, job => job.status === \"dead\");\n\n    const response = await retryJob(base, jobId);\n    assert.strictEqual(response.status, 200);\n    assert.deepStrictEqual(await response.json(), {\n      ok: true,\n      status: \"pending\",\n      retries: 1,\n    });\n\n    const { job, state } = await waitForJob(base, jobId, item => item.status === \"done\");\n    assert.deepStrictEqual(\n      {\n        status: job.status,\n        attempts: job.attempts,\n        lastError: job.lastError,\n        retries: job.retries,\n        attemptsSinceRetry: job.attemptsSinceRetry,\n      },\n      {\n        status: \"done\",\n        attempts: 4,\n        lastError: null,\n        retries: 1,\n        attemptsSinceRetry: 1,\n      },\n    );\n    assert.deepStrictEqual(\n      state.approvals.find(item => item.jobId === jobId)?.action,\n      {\n        to: \"test@example.com\",\n        subject: \"Recovered action\",\n        body: \"The retry completed.\",\n      },\n    );\n  });\n});\n\ntest(\"2. A dead job, retried, still failing → dead again after exactly 3 new attempts, with cumulative attempts visible on the record\", async () => {\n  await withServer(4752, async ({ base }) => {\n    const eventId = \"retry-still-failing\";\n    const jobId = `job-${eventId}`;\n    await postEvent(base, eventId, { failTimes: 99 });\n    await waitForJob(base, jobId, job => job.status === \"dead\");\n\n    const response = await retryJob(base, jobId);\n    assert.strictEqual(response.status, 200);\n    assert.deepStrictEqual(await response.json(), {\n      ok: true,\n      status: \"pending\",\n      retries: 1,\n    });\n\n    const { job } = await waitForJob(\n      base,\n      jobId,\n      item => item.status === \"dead\" && item.retries === 1,\n    );\n    assert.deepStrictEqual(\n      {\n        status: job.status,\n        attempts: job.attempts,\n        lastError: job.lastError,\n        retries: job.retries,\n        attemptsSinceRetry: job.attemptsSinceRetry,\n      },\n      {\n        status: \"dead\",\n        attempts: 6,\n        lastError: \"simulated failure on attempt 6\",\n        retries: 1,\n        attemptsSinceRetry: 3,\n      },\n    );\n  });\n});\n\ntest(\"3. Retry of a non-dead job (pending or done) → refused with 409, record unchanged\", async () => {\n  await withServer(4753, async ({ base }) => {\n    const eventId = \"retry-pending\";\n    const jobId = `job-${eventId}`;\n    await postEvent(base, eventId);\n    const before = (await getState(base)).jobs.find(item => item.id === jobId);\n\n    const response = await retryJob(base, jobId);\n    assert.strictEqual(response.status, 409);\n    assert.deepStrictEqual(await response.json(), {\n      ok: false,\n      error: \"only dead jobs can be retried (status: pending)\",\n    });\n    const after = (await getState(base)).jobs.find(item => item.id === jobId);\n    assert.strictEqual(JSON.stringify(after), JSON.stringify(before));\n    assert.strictEqual(after.retries, 0);\n    assert.strictEqual(after.attemptsSinceRetry, 0);\n  }, 60_000);\n\n  await withServer(4754, async ({ base }) => {\n    const eventId = \"retry-done\";\n    const jobId = `job-${eventId}`;\n    await postEvent(base, eventId);\n    const { job: before } = await waitForJob(base, jobId, job => job.status === \"done\");\n\n    const response = await retryJob(base, jobId);\n    assert.strictEqual(response.status, 409);\n    assert.deepStrictEqual(await response.json(), {\n      ok: false,\n      error: \"only dead jobs can be retried (status: done)\",\n    });\n    const after = (await getState(base)).jobs.find(item => item.id === jobId);\n    assert.strictEqual(JSON.stringify(after), JSON.stringify(before));\n    assert.strictEqual(after.retries, 0);\n    assert.strictEqual(after.attemptsSinceRetry, 1);\n  });\n});\n\ntest(\"4. Kill the server right after a retry is accepted; on restart the re-queued job is processed\", async () => {\n  const port = 4755;\n  const base = `http://localhost:${port}`;\n  const dataDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"relay-retry-dead-restart-test-\"));\n  let proc = startServer(port, dataDir, 1_000);\n\n  try {\n    await waitForHealth(base);\n    const eventId = \"retry-crash-recovery\";\n    const jobId = `job-${eventId}`;\n    await postEvent(base, eventId, { failTimes: 3, subject: \"Recovered after restart\" });\n    await waitForJob(base, jobId, job => job.status === \"dead\", 50);\n\n    const response = await retryJob(base, jobId);\n    assert.strictEqual(response.status, 200);\n    assert.deepStrictEqual(await response.json(), {\n      ok: true,\n      status: \"pending\",\n      retries: 1,\n    });\n    await stopServer(proc);\n\n    proc = startServer(port, dataDir, 50);\n    await waitForHealth(base);\n    const { job, state } = await waitForJob(base, jobId, item => item.status === \"done\");\n    assert.deepStrictEqual(\n      {\n        attempts: job.attempts,\n        retries: job.retries,\n        attemptsSinceRetry: job.attemptsSinceRetry,\n      },\n      { attempts: 4, retries: 1, attemptsSinceRetry: 1 },\n    );\n    assert.strictEqual(\n      state.approvals.some(item => item.jobId === jobId && item.action.subject === \"Recovered after restart\"),\n      true,\n    );\n  } finally {\n    await stopServer(proc);\n    fs.rmSync(dataDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"Unknown job → 404 with exactly the frozen no-such-job response\", async () => {\n  await withServer(4756, async ({ base }) => {\n    const response = await retryJob(base, \"job-unknown\");\n    assert.strictEqual(response.status, 404);\n    assert.deepStrictEqual(await response.json(), {\n      ok: false,\n      error: \"no such job\",\n    });\n  });\n});\n{\n  \"name\": \"relay-conformance\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"description\": \"Nysa-shaped conformance product for the software factory kit. Zero dependencies.\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"start\": \"node server.js\",\n    \"test\": \"node --test tests/*.test.js\"\n  }\n}\nb1d9ddf T-104: add failing retry-dead acceptance tests\n conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js | 259 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md     |   1 +\n 2 files changed, 260 insertions(+)\ncommit b1d9ddf867055ae47e9a13ecbd55dad34940705f\nAuthor:     hermes-dispatcher <hermes-dispatcher@nysa-company.local>\nAuthorDate: Sun Jul 12 23:06:01 2026 -0600\nCommit:     hermes-dispatcher <hermes-dispatcher@nysa-company.local>\nCommitDate: Sun Jul 12 23:06:01 2026 -0600\n\n    T-104: add failing retry-dead acceptance tests\n\ndiff --git a/conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js b/conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..f7d7737\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js\n@@ -0,0 +1,259 @@\n+const { test } = require(\"node:test\");\n+const assert = require(\"node:assert\");\n+const { spawn } = require(\"node:child_process\");\n+const fs = require(\"node:fs\");\n+const path = require(\"node:path\");\n+const os = require(\"node:os\");\n+\n+const SERVER = path.join(__dirname, \"..\", \"server.js\");\n+\n+function startServer(port, dataDir, workerMs = 50) {\n+  return spawn(process.execPath, [SERVER], {\n+    env: {\n+      ...process.env,\n+      PORT: String(port),\n+      DATA_DIR: dataDir,\n+      WORKER_MS: String(workerMs),\n+      ALLOWLIST: \"test@example.com\",\n+    },\n+    stdio: \"ignore\",\n+  });\n+}\n+\n+async function waitForHealth(base, tries = 50) {\n+  for (let i = 0; i < tries; i++) {\n+    try {\n+      if ((await fetch(`${base}/health`)).ok) return;\n+    } catch { /* not up yet */ }\n+    await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));\n+  }\n+  throw new Error(\"server did not come up\");\n+}\n+\n+async function stopServer(proc) {\n+  if (proc.exitCode !== null || proc.signalCode !== null) return;\n+  const exited = new Promise(resolve => proc.once(\"exit\", resolve));\n+  proc.kill(\"SIGKILL\");\n+  await exited;\n+}\n+\n+async function withServer(port, run, workerMs = 50) {\n+  const base = `http://localhost:${port}`;\n+  const dataDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"relay-retry-dead-test-\"));\n+  const proc = startServer(port, dataDir, workerMs);\n+\n+  try {\n+    await waitForHealth(base);\n+    await run({ base, dataDir, proc });\n+  } finally {\n+    await stopServer(proc);\n+    fs.rmSync(dataDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n+  }\n+}\n+\n+async function postEvent(base, id, payload = {}) {\n+  const response = await fetch(`${base}/webhook/event`, {\n+    method: \"POST\",\n+    headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n+    body: JSON.stringify({ id, payload }),\n+  });\n+  assert.strictEqual(response.status, 200);\n+  return response.json();\n+}\n+\n+function retryJob(base, jobId) {\n+  return fetch(`${base}/api/jobs/${jobId}/retry`, { method: \"POST\" });\n+}\n+\n+async function getState(base) {\n+  return (await fetch(`${base}/api/state`)).json();\n+}\n+\n+async function waitForJob(base, jobId, predicate, tries = 100) {\n+  for (let i = 0; i < tries; i++) {\n+    const state = await getState(base);\n+    const job = state.jobs.find(item => item.id === jobId);\n+    if (job && predicate(job, state)) return { job, state };\n+    await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));\n+  }\n+  throw new Error(`job ${jobId} did not reach the expected state`);\n+}\n+\n+test(\"1. A dead job, retried → pending again; a job whose cause is fixed completes and produces its proposed action as normal\", async () => {\n+  await withServer(4751, async ({ base }) => {\n+    const eventId = \"retry-then-complete\";\n+    const jobId = `job-${eventId}`;\n+    await postEvent(base, eventId, {\n+      failTimes: 3,\n+      to: \"test@example.com\",\n+      subject: \"Recovered action\",\n+      body: \"The retry completed.\",\n+    });\n+    await waitForJob(base, jobId, job => job.status === \"dead\");\n+\n+    const response = await retryJob(base, jobId);\n+    assert.strictEqual(response.status, 200);\n+    assert.deepStrictEqual(await response.json(), {\n+      ok: true,\n+      status: \"pending\",\n+      retries: 1,\n+    });\n+\n+    const { job, state } = await waitForJob(base, jobId, item => item.status === \"done\");\n+    assert.deepStrictEqual(\n+      {\n+        status: job.status,\n+        attempts: job.attempts,\n+        lastError: job.lastError,\n+        retries: job.retries,\n+        attemptsSinceRetry: job.attemptsSinceRetry,\n+      },\n+      {\n+        status: \"done\",\n+        attempts: 4,\n+        lastError: null,\n+        retries: 1,\n+        attemptsSinceRetry: 1,\n+      },\n+    );\n+    assert.deepStrictEqual(\n+      state.approvals.find(item => item.jobId === jobId)?.action,\n+      {\n+        to: \"test@example.com\",\n+        subject: \"Recovered action\",\n+        body: \"The retry completed.\",\n+      },\n+    );\n+  });\n+});\n+\n+test(\"2. A dead job, retried, still failing → dead again after exactly 3 new attempts, with cumulative attempts visible on the record\", async () => {\n+  await withServer(4752, async ({ base }) => {\n+    const eventId = \"retry-still-failing\";\n+    const jobId = `job-${eventId}`;\n+    await postEvent(base, eventId, { failTimes: 99 });\n+    await waitForJob(base, jobId, job => job.status === \"dead\");\n+\n+    const response = await retryJob(base, jobId);\n+    assert.strictEqual(response.status, 200);\n+    assert.deepStrictEqual(await response.json(), {\n+      ok: true,\n+      status: \"pending\",\n+      retries: 1,\n+    });\n+\n+    const { job } = await waitForJob(\n+      base,\n+      jobId,\n+      item => item.status === \"dead\" && item.retries === 1,\n+    );\n+    assert.deepStrictEqual(\n+      {\n+        status: job.status,\n+        attempts: job.attempts,\n+        lastError: job.lastError,\n+        retries: job.retries,\n+        attemptsSinceRetry: job.attemptsSinceRetry,\n+      },\n+      {\n+        status: \"dead\",\n+        attempts: 6,\n+        lastError: \"simulated failure on attempt 6\",\n+        retries: 1,\n+        attemptsSinceRetry: 3,\n+      },\n+    );\n+  });\n+});\n+\n+test(\"3. Retry of a non-dead job (pending or done) → refused with 409, record unchanged\", async () => {\n+  await withServer(4753, async ({ base }) => {\n+    const eventId = \"retry-pending\";\n+    const jobId = `job-${eventId}`;\n+    await postEvent(base, eventId);\n+    const before = (await getState(base)).jobs.find(item => item.id === jobId);\n+\n+    const response = await retryJob(base, jobId);\n+    assert.strictEqual(response.status, 409);\n+    assert.deepStrictEqual(await response.json(), {\n+      ok: false,\n+      error: \"only dead jobs can be retried (status: pending)\",\n+    });\n+    const after = (await getState(base)).jobs.find(item => item.id === jobId);\n+    assert.strictEqual(JSON.stringify(after), JSON.stringify(before));\n+    assert.strictEqual(after.retries, 0);\n+    assert.strictEqual(after.attemptsSinceRetry, 0);\n+  }, 60_000);\n+\n+  await withServer(4754, async ({ base }) => {\n+    const eventId = \"retry-done\";\n+    const jobId = `job-${eventId}`;\n+    await postEvent(base, eventId);\n+    const { job: before } = await waitForJob(base, jobId, job => job.status === \"done\");\n+\n+    const response = await retryJob(base, jobId);\n+    assert.strictEqual(response.status, 409);\n+    assert.deepStrictEqual(await response.json(), {\n+      ok: false,\n+      error: \"only dead jobs can be retried (status: done)\",\n+    });\n+    const after = (await getState(base)).jobs.find(item => item.id === jobId);\n+    assert.strictEqual(JSON.stringify(after), JSON.stringify(before));\n+    assert.strictEqual(after.retries, 0);\n+    assert.strictEqual(after.attemptsSinceRetry, 1);\n+  });\n+});\n+\n+test(\"4. Kill the server right after a retry is accepted; on restart the re-queued job is processed\", async () => {\n+  const port = 4755;\n+  const base = `http://localhost:${port}`;\n+  const dataDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"relay-retry-dead-restart-test-\"));\n+  let proc = startServer(port, dataDir, 1_000);\n+\n+  try {\n+    await waitForHealth(base);\n+    const eventId = \"retry-crash-recovery\";\n+    const jobId = `job-${eventId}`;\n+    await postEvent(base, eventId, { failTimes: 3, subject: \"Recovered after restart\" });\n+    await waitForJob(base, jobId, job => job.status === \"dead\", 50);\n+\n+    const response = await retryJob(base, jobId);\n+    assert.strictEqual(response.status, 200);\n+    assert.deepStrictEqual(await response.json(), {\n+      ok: true,\n+      status: \"pending\",\n+      retries: 1,\n+    });\n+    await stopServer(proc);\n+\n+    proc = startServer(port, dataDir, 50);\n+    await waitForHealth(base);\n+    const { job, state } = await waitForJob(base, jobId, item => item.status === \"done\");\n+    assert.deepStrictEqual(\n+      {\n+        attempts: job.attempts,\n+        retries: job.retries,\n+        attemptsSinceRetry: job.attemptsSinceRetry,\n+      },\n+      { attempts: 4, retries: 1, attemptsSinceRetry: 1 },\n+    );\n+    assert.strictEqual(\n+      state.approvals.some(item => item.jobId === jobId && item.action.subject === \"Recovered after restart\"),\n+      true,\n+    );\n+  } finally {\n+    await stopServer(proc);\n+    fs.rmSync(dataDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n+  }\n+});\n+\n+test(\"Unknown job → 404 with exactly the frozen no-such-job response\", async () => {\n+  await withServer(4756, async ({ base }) => {\n+    const response = await retryJob(base, \"job-unknown\");\n+    assert.strictEqual(response.status, 404);\n+    assert.deepStrictEqual(await response.json(), {\n+      ok: false,\n+      error: \"no such job\",\n+    });\n+  });\n+});\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"The frozen contract is clear, and the existing file already maps one named test to each acceptance criterion. I’ll strengthen those existing AC1/AC2 tests rather than add overlapping criteria: AC1 will pause worker advancement via a restart with a long tick interval and inspect the persisted post-`200` record; AC2 will execute a complete second dead→retry cycle and verify the exact `retries: 2` transition and cumulative counters. The unrelated untracked factory run artifacts will remain untouched."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,300p' conformance/app/server.js; git status --porcelain=v1; git branch --show-current; git diff --check\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,300p' conformance/app/server.js; git status --porcelain=v1; git branch --show-current; git diff --check\"","aggregated_output":"// Relay — conformance product. Zero dependencies; Node 18+.\n// See ../SPEC.md for the behavior contract this implements.\nconst http = require(\"node:http\");\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst path = require(\"node:path\");\nconst crypto = require(\"node:crypto\");\n\nconst PORT = Number(process.env.PORT || 4700);\nconst DATA_DIR = process.env.DATA_DIR || path.join(__dirname, \"data\");\nconst STATE_FILE = path.join(DATA_DIR, \"state.json\");\nconst ALLOWLIST = (process.env.ALLOWLIST || \"test@example.com\").split(\",\").map(s => s.trim());\nconst WORKER_MS = Number(process.env.WORKER_MS || 200);\nconst MAX_ATTEMPTS = 3;\n\n// ---------- durable state ----------\nlet state = { events: [], jobs: [], approvals: [], outbox: [] };\n\nfunction loadState() {\n  try {\n    state = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(STATE_FILE, \"utf8\"));\n  } catch {\n    /* first boot or unreadable: start clean */\n  }\n}\n\n// Atomic persist: write temp file, then rename. A crash mid-write never\n// corrupts the previous good state.\nfunction persist() {\n  fs.mkdirSync(DATA_DIR, { recursive: true });\n  const tmp = STATE_FILE + \".\" + crypto.randomBytes(4).toString(\"hex\");\n  fs.writeFileSync(tmp, JSON.stringify(state, null, 2));\n  fs.renameSync(tmp, STATE_FILE);\n}\n\n// ---------- domain ----------\nfunction acceptEvent(evt) {\n  if (!evt || typeof evt.id !== \"string\" || !evt.id) return { ok: false, error: \"missing event id\" };\n  const existing = state.events.find(e => e.id === evt.id);\n  if (existing) return { ok: true, duplicate: true, eventId: evt.id }; // idempotent ack\n  state.events.push({ id: evt.id, type: evt.type || \"generic\", payload: evt.payload || {}, receivedAt: new Date().toISOString() });\n  state.jobs.push({\n    id: \"job-\" + evt.id,\n    eventId: evt.id,\n    status: \"pending\", // pending | done | dead\n    attempts: 0,\n    lastError: null,\n    retries: 0,\n    attemptsSinceRetry: 0,\n  });\n  persist();\n  return { ok: true, duplicate: false, eventId: evt.id };\n}\n\nfunction processJob(job) {\n  const evt = state.events.find(e => e.id === job.eventId);\n  job.attempts += 1;\n  job.attemptsSinceRetry += 1;\n  // Simulated transient/permanent failure: payload.failTimes = number of\n  // attempts that must fail before success (99 = effectively permanent).\n  const failTimes = Number(evt?.payload?.failTimes || 0);\n  if (job.attempts <= failTimes) {\n    job.lastError = `simulated failure on attempt ${job.attempts}`;\n    if (job.attemptsSinceRetry >= MAX_ATTEMPTS) job.status = \"dead\";\n    persist();\n    return;\n  }\n  // Success: produce a proposed action requiring approval. Nothing sends here.\n  state.approvals.push({\n    id: \"appr-\" + job.eventId,\n    jobId: job.id,\n    action: {\n      to: evt?.payload?.to || ALLOWLIST[0],\n      subject: evt?.payload?.subject || `Follow-up for ${job.eventId}`,\n      body: evt?.payload?.body || \"Proposed by Relay worker.\",\n    },\n    status: \"pending\", // pending | sent | rejected | blocked_recipient\n    proposedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n  });\n  job.status = \"done\";\n  job.lastError = null;\n  persist();\n}\n\nfunction workerTick() {\n  const job = state.jobs.find(j => j.status === \"pending\");\n  if (job) processJob(job);\n}\n\nfunction approve(id) {\n  const appr = state.approvals.find(a => a.id === id);\n  if (!appr) return { ok: false, code: 404, error: \"no such approval\" };\n  if (appr.status !== \"pending\") return { ok: false, code: 409, error: `already ${appr.status}` };\n  if (!ALLOWLIST.includes(appr.action.to)) {\n    appr.status = \"blocked_recipient\";\n    persist();\n    return { ok: false, code: 403, error: `recipient ${appr.action.to} not on allowlist — send blocked`, status: appr.status };\n  }\n  state.outbox.push({ ...appr.action, approvalId: appr.id, sentAt: new Date().toISOString() });\n  appr.status = \"sent\";\n  persist();\n  return { ok: true, status: \"sent\" };\n}\n\nfunction reject(id, body) {\n  const appr = state.approvals.find(a => a.id === id);\n  if (!appr) return { ok: false, code: 404, error: \"no such approval\" };\n  if (appr.status !== \"pending\") return { ok: false, code: 409, error: `already ${appr.status}` };\n  const reason = typeof body?.reason === \"string\" ? body.reason : null;\n  appr.status = \"rejected\";\n  appr.reason = reason;\n  persist();\n  return { ok: true, status: \"rejected\", reason };\n}\n\nfunction retryJob(id) {\n  const job = state.jobs.find(j => j.id === id);\n  if (!job) return { ok: false, code: 404, error: \"no such job\" };\n  if (job.status !== \"dead\") {\n    return { ok: false, code: 409, error: `only dead jobs can be retried (status: ${job.status})` };\n  }\n  job.status = \"pending\";\n  job.attemptsSinceRetry = 0;\n  job.retries += 1;\n  persist();\n  return { ok: true, code: 200, status: \"pending\", retries: job.retries };\n}\n\n// ---------- http ----------\nfunction json(res, code, obj) {\n  res.writeHead(code, { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" });\n  res.end(JSON.stringify(obj));\n}\n\nfunction readBody(req) {\n  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n    let data = \"\";\n    req.on(\"data\", c => { data += c; if (data.length > 1e6) req.destroy(); });\n    req.on(\"end\", () => { try { resolve(data ? JSON.parse(data) : {}); } catch (e) { reject(e); } });\n    req.on(\"error\", reject);\n  });\n}\n\nfunction ui() {\n  const row = (cells) => `<tr>${cells.map(c => `<td>${String(c)}</td>`).join(\"\")}</tr>`;\n  return `<!doctype html><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Relay</title>\n<style>body{font-family:system-ui;margin:2rem;max-width:60rem}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin-bottom:1.5rem}td,th{border:1px solid #ddd;padding:.4rem .6rem;text-align:left;font-size:14px}h2{margin:.2rem 0 .4rem}</style>\n<h1>Relay</h1>\n<h2>Events (${state.events.length})</h2><table><tr><th>id</th><th>type</th><th>received</th></tr>${state.events.map(e => row([e.id, e.type, e.receivedAt])).join(\"\")}</table>\n<h2>Jobs</h2><table><tr><th>id</th><th>status</th><th>attempts</th><th>lastError</th></tr>${state.jobs.map(j => row([j.id, j.status, j.attempts, j.lastError || \"\"])).join(\"\")}</table>\n<h2>Approvals</h2><table><tr><th>id</th><th>to</th><th>subject</th><th>status</th></tr>${state.approvals.map(a => row([a.id, a.action.to, a.action.subject, a.status])).join(\"\")}</table>\n<h2>Outbox (sandboxed)</h2><table><tr><th>to</th><th>subject</th><th>sentAt</th></tr>${state.outbox.map(o => row([o.to, o.subject, o.sentAt])).join(\"\")}</table>`;\n}\n\nconst server = http.createServer(async (req, res) => {\n  const url = new URL(req.url, `http://localhost:${PORT}`);\n  try {\n    if (req.method === \"GET\" && url.pathname === \"/\") {\n      res.writeHead(200, { \"Content-Type\": \"text/html\" });\n      return res.end(ui());\n    }\n    if (req.method === \"GET\" && url.pathname === \"/api/state\") return json(res, 200, state);\n    if (req.method === \"GET\" && url.pathname === \"/health\") {\n      const queue = { pending: 0, done: 0, dead: 0 };\n      for (const j of state.jobs) if (j.status in queue) queue[j.status] += 1;\n      const approvals = { pending: 0, sent: 0, rejected: 0, blocked_recipient: 0 };\n      for (const a of state.approvals) if (a.status in approvals) approvals[a.status] += 1;\n      return json(res, 200, { ok: true, queue, approvals });\n    }\n    if (req.method === \"POST\" && url.pathname === \"/webhook/event\") {\n      const body = await readBody(req);\n      const result = acceptEvent(body);\n      return json(res, result.ok ? 200 : 400, result);\n    }\n    const mApprove = url.pathname.match(/^\\/api\\/approvals\\/([^/]+)\\/approve$/);\n    if (req.method === \"POST\" && mApprove) {\n      const result = approve(mApprove[1]);\n      return json(res, result.ok ? 200 : result.code, result);\n    }\n    const mReject = url.pathname.match(/^\\/api\\/approvals\\/([^/]+)\\/reject$/);\n    if (req.method === \"POST\" && mReject) {\n      const body = await readBody(req);\n      const { code, ...result } = reject(mReject[1], body);\n      return json(res, result.ok ? 200 : code, result);\n    }\n    const mRetry = url.pathname.match(/^\\/api\\/jobs\\/([^/]+)\\/retry$/);\n    if (req.method === \"POST\" && mRetry) {\n      const { code, ...result } = retryJob(mRetry[1]);\n      return json(res, code, result);\n    }\n    json(res, 404, { error: \"not found\" });\n  } catch (e) {\n    json(res, 400, { error: String(e.message || e) });\n  }\n});\n\nloadState();\nsetInterval(workerTick, WORKER_MS);\nserver.listen(PORT, () => console.log(`relay listening on :${PORT} (data: ${DATA_DIR})`));\n?? conformance/factory/runs/1783918994-98019.out\n?? conformance/factory/runs/1783919207-99006.out\n?? conformance/factory/runs/1783919328-99557.out\n?? conformance/factory/runs/1783919498-394.out\n?? conformance/factory/runs/1783919498-394.pid\nticket/T-104-retry-dead-job\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
